  "term": "second-order interaction",
  "definition": "Second-order interaction is the pairwise relationship between variables that a model uses to capture how multivariate exponential signals are connected. In this source, it refers to estimating those interactions for the rate intensity parameters in logarithmic space so the underlying correlation structure of the signals can be represented.",
